1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:05,930
The fingers reach the cup correctly, yet the cup falls as soon as the wrist moves.
手指准确到达杯子，手腕一动，杯子却掉了。

2
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:10,050
That failure does not necessarily mean the geometric mapping was wrong.
这种失败，并不一定说明几何映射本身错了。

3
00:00:10,430 --> 00:00:16,150
The required grip must also withstand gravity, acceleration, and changing contact conditions.
实际抓握还要承受重力、加速度，以及不断变化的接触条件。

4
00:00:16,630 --> 00:00:21,650
A reference trajectory tells us where the robot should go, not how forces will get it there.
参考轨迹告诉我们机器人应到哪里，却没解决力如何让它到达。

5
00:00:21,890 --> 00:00:26,075
This chapter follows methods that add physical execution to human motion transfer.
这一章，我们来看如何把物理执行加入人体动作迁移。

6
00:00:26,090 --> 00:00:31,910
We will separate simulated feasibility, learned feedback, and demonstrated real robot success.
我们会区分仿真可行、学习到的反馈，以及已展示的真机成功。

7
00:00:32,497 --> 00:00:37,657
Suppose a retargeter outputs a desired joint angle, which we call the reference.
假设重定向器输出一个期望关节角，我们把它称为参考。

8
00:00:38,157 --> 00:00:43,317
A low-level controller compares that reference with the measured angle and generates motor effort.
低层控制器比较参考与测量角度，再产生电机驱动力。

9
00:00:43,777 --> 00:00:49,897
The resulting motion depends on inertia, friction, contact geometry, and the controller itself.
最终运动取决于惯量、摩擦、接触几何，以及控制器本身。

10
00:00:50,237 --> 00:00:54,757
Directly placing a simulated hand into the reference pose skips much of this process.
直接把仿真手摆进参考姿态，会跳过其中大量过程。

11
00:00:55,017 --> 00:00:59,202
So a clean animation is not automatically a dynamically feasible rollout.
所以，一段干净的动画，并不自动等于动力学可行的执行。

12
00:00:59,217 --> 00:01:04,857
Our diagrams distinguish the target, the applied action, and the motion actually achieved.
这里的示意图会分开显示目标、施加的动作，以及实际产生的运动。

13
00:01:05,422 --> 00:01:11,142
QuasiSim starts from a difficult problem: optimizing through contact is often unstable.
QuasiSim 从一个困难出发：经过接触过程的优化常常不稳定。

14
00:01:11,802 --> 00:01:15,862
A tiny change can make a finger touch, miss, or collide with an object.
一个微小变化，就可能让手指接触、错过，或撞上物体。

15
00:01:16,302 --> 00:01:21,642
In the original figure, the hand is temporarily relaxed into a parameterized point-set model.
原论文图中，手暂时被放松为一个参数化点集模型。

16
00:01:22,122 --> 00:01:26,462
Adjustable spring and damping behavior makes early contact optimization easier.
可调节的弹簧与阻尼行为，让初期接触优化更容易。

17
00:01:26,962 --> 00:01:32,087
A residual physics component models effects that the analytical simulator does not capture well.
残差物理模块用来补偿解析模拟器难以准确描述的效应。

18
00:01:32,102 --> 00:01:37,982
These changes concern the physics model used for optimization, not just a fingertip distance loss.
这些变化针对的是优化所用的物理模型，而不只是一个指尖距离损失。

19
00:01:38,587 --> 00:01:41,612
Read the lower row of that figure from left to right.
沿着原图下方，从左向右看这个过程。

20
00:01:41,627 --> 00:01:46,907
Optimization first benefits from relaxed constraints, then restores stricter dynamics.
优化先借助放松的约束，再恢复更严格的动力学条件。

21
00:01:47,467 --> 00:01:51,907
The final trajectory must work after those earlier simplifications are removed.
移除这些前期简化后，最终轨迹仍必须能够执行。

22
00:01:52,267 --> 00:01:57,512
This is an offline trajectory-generation strategy, not an instant camera-to-hand mapping.
这是一种离线轨迹生成策略，不是即时的摄像头到机器人手映射。

23
00:01:57,527 --> 00:02:03,772
Its baselines include a modified DGrasp tracking method, whose task differs from original DGrasp.
其基线包含改造后的 DGrasp 跟踪方法，任务设定与原始 DGrasp 不同。

24
00:02:03,787 --> 00:02:08,387
Preserve that modification and the sequence-dependent cost when presenting the comparison.
展示比较时，要保留这个改造说明，以及随序列变化的计算成本。

25
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:15,260
ManipTrans takes another route: first train a reusable policy to imitate human hand motion.
ManipTrans 走另一条路线：先训练可复用策略，模仿人体手部运动。

26
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:19,340
In this original diagram, the upper model is the hand imitator.
在原论文图中，上方模型就是手部模仿器。

27
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:25,040
It observes the reference motion and the simulated robot's state, then produces coarse actions.
它观察参考运动与仿真机器人的状态，再输出粗略动作。

28
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:30,220
Training rewards wrist tracking, finger tracking, and smooth motion before adding objects.
加入物体前，训练奖励手腕跟踪、手指跟踪与平滑运动。

29
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:35,725
This stage can use hand-only motion data, which is easier to collect than complete interactions.
这一阶段能使用单独的手部运动数据，其采集比完整交互更容易。

30
00:02:35,740 --> 00:02:40,740
The pretrained policy becomes a starting point for many later manipulation transfers.
这个预训练策略，随后成为多次操作迁移的起点。

31
00:02:41,411 --> 00:02:46,951
Now follow the lower branch, where object trajectories and interaction information enter.
再看下方分支，物体轨迹与交互信息从这里进入。

32
00:02:47,411 --> 00:02:51,791
A second policy adds a corrective action to the hand imitator's proposed action.
第二个策略，把修正动作加在手部模仿器提出的动作上。

33
00:02:52,151 --> 00:02:57,811
It observes object state and shape, hand-object relationships, and simulated contact forces.
它观察物体状态与形状、手物关系，以及仿真接触力。

34
00:02:58,191 --> 00:03:02,931
The action space includes joint position targets and a floating wrist force in simulation.
动作空间包含关节位置目标，以及仿真中浮动手腕所施加的力。

35
00:03:03,431 --> 00:03:08,536
This is a physical control problem, rather than simply refining an inverse-kinematics pose.
这是物理控制问题，而不只是进一步修正一个逆运动学姿态。

36
00:03:08,551 --> 00:03:14,391
A good reference reduces the search burden, while feedback can compensate for imperfect interaction.
好的参考减少探索负担，而反馈可以补偿不完美的交互。

37
00:03:15,055 --> 00:03:22,075
ManipTrans compares retargeting only, reinforcement learning only, and retargeting with residuals.
ManipTrans 比较仅重定向、仅强化学习，以及重定向加残差。

38
00:03:22,095 --> 00:03:24,855
Its full method adds the reusable hand imitator.
完整方法则加入可复用的手部模仿器。

39
00:03:25,295 --> 00:03:29,555
The third baseline matters because it already includes learned physical correction.
第三个基线尤其重要，因为它本身已经包含学习得到的物理修正。

40
00:03:29,795 --> 00:03:33,595
Comparing against it tests the benefit of the reusable hand imitator.
与它比较，才能检验可复用手部模仿器带来的收益。

41
00:03:33,935 --> 00:03:39,460
The study uses selected OakInk sequences, with success defined by several tracking thresholds.
研究使用筛选后的 OakInk 序列，成功由多个跟踪阈值共同定义。

42
00:03:39,475 --> 00:03:45,155
Tracking errors cover successful rollouts only, so inspect success rate alongside error.
跟踪误差只统计成功执行，因此要把成功率与误差一起看。

43
00:03:45,315 --> 00:03:49,535
Otherwise, a method that solves only easy cases can look deceptively accurate.
否则，一个只完成简单样例的方法，也可能显得异常准确。

44
00:03:50,048 --> 00:03:55,588
The mouse-rotation example adapts quickly once the pretrained hand imitator is available.
在已有预训练手部模仿器后，转动鼠标的样例可以较快适配。

45
00:03:56,348 --> 00:04:00,948
That short adaptation time does not include the original general-purpose pretraining.
这段较短的适配时间，不包含最初的通用预训练。

46
00:04:01,508 --> 00:04:05,728
The appendix reports roughly one and a half days for that reusable stage.
附录报告，这个可复用阶段大约需要一天半。

47
00:04:06,088 --> 00:04:11,508
Keep one-time preparation, per-sequence training, and online policy inference in separate columns.
请把一次性准备、逐序列训练和在线策略推理放在不同列里。

48
00:04:11,888 --> 00:04:17,453
Also check embodiment details: simulated joints may have more freedom than the physical mechanism.
还要检查构型细节：仿真关节可能比真实机构拥有更多自由度。

49
00:04:17,468 --> 00:04:23,248
ManipTrans fits simulated Inspire motion to the more constrained hardware before real execution.
ManipTrans 在真实执行前，会把仿真 Inspire 运动拟合到约束更多的硬件。

50
00:04:23,936 --> 00:04:29,556
SPIDER avoids training a new policy for every trajectory in its core retargeting solver.
SPIDER 的核心重定向求解器，避免为每条轨迹训练一个新策略。

51
00:04:29,936 --> 00:04:35,096
The original pipeline first extracts hand motion, object geometry, and object motion.
原论文管线先提取手部运动、物体几何与物体运动。

52
00:04:35,516 --> 00:04:40,476
A kinematic robot reference then guides parallel simulations of candidate action sequences.
机器人运动学参考随后引导多个候选动作序列的并行仿真。

53
00:04:40,796 --> 00:04:45,356
It scores those rollouts and gradually focuses its search around promising candidates.
它给这些执行评分，再逐渐把搜索集中到更有希望的候选附近。

54
00:04:45,736 --> 00:04:51,296
Its output is a physically simulated control trajectory, not a universal learned hand mapper.
它输出的是经过物理仿真的控制轨迹，而不是通用的学习式手部映射器。

55
00:04:51,316 --> 00:04:56,236
Robustification and later policy learning are additional stages with their own purposes and costs.
鲁棒化与后续策略学习属于额外阶段，各有自己的目的和成本。

56
00:04:56,913 --> 00:05:02,613
Two grasps can move an object along similar paths while using different contact regions.
两种抓法可能让物体走相似路径，却使用不同的接触区域。

57
00:05:03,213 --> 00:05:08,873
In this figure, SPIDER illustrates why unconstrained sampling may choose the unintended grasp.
这张图解释了为什么不加引导的采样，可能选到不符合原意的抓法。

58
00:05:09,753 --> 00:05:13,953
Contact guidance temporarily adds virtual constraints around the desired interaction.
接触引导在期望交互关系附近，暂时加入虚拟约束。

59
00:05:14,433 --> 00:05:18,413
This makes the preferred contact mode easier to discover during optimization.
这样，优化过程更容易发现期望的接触模式。

60
00:05:19,033 --> 00:05:24,233
The assistance is gradually relaxed, and noisy, unstable contact annotations can be filtered.
这些辅助会逐渐减弱，带噪或不稳定的接触标注也可以被过滤。

61
00:05:24,573 --> 00:05:29,153
Inspect the final unassisted rollout before claiming that contact is physically feasible.
宣称接触物理可行之前，要检查最终的无辅助执行。

62
00:05:29,902 --> 00:05:35,622
SPIDER version three compares methods with matched simulators, datasets, and hand models.
SPIDER 第三版在对齐的模拟器、数据集与手模型下比较方法。

63
00:05:36,102 --> 00:05:41,942
Its object tracking metric is ADD-AUC, integrating accuracy across a range of distance thresholds.
其物体跟踪指标是 ADD-AUC，把一段距离阈值范围内的准确度积分。

64
00:05:42,462 --> 00:05:45,847
It is not the same quantity as a single task success percentage.
它与某个单一任务的成功百分比，不是同一个量。

65
00:05:45,862 --> 00:05:50,982
Reported frames per second measure generated frames divided by total generation time.
报告的每秒帧数，是生成帧数除以全部生成时间。

66
00:05:51,482 --> 00:05:54,967
They do not mean the system can process a live camera at that rate.
它们不代表系统能以这个速率实时处理摄像头。

67
00:05:54,982 --> 00:06:00,002
Read variance, failures, and guidance cost before choosing a generator for your dataset.
为数据集选择生成器前，要查看方差、失败情况与引导成本。

68
00:06:00,749 --> 00:06:07,429
DexH2R starts with kinematic primitive actions, then learns corrections using task information.
DexH2R 从运动学基础动作开始，再利用任务信息学习修正。

69
00:06:07,809 --> 00:06:13,229
In its original figure, the primitive and residual branches meet before the final robot action.
原图中，基础动作与残差分支在最终机器人动作之前汇合。

70
00:06:13,549 --> 00:06:19,249
The policy observes robot and object state, binary contact, and future reference goals.
策略观察机器人与物体状态、二值接触，以及未来参考目标。

71
00:06:19,509 --> 00:06:25,094
Its primitive uses joint-angle changes, so check action conventions before combining modules.
它的基础动作使用关节角变化量，因此组合模块前要核对动作定义。

72
00:06:25,109 --> 00:06:31,989
This is the task-oriented DexH2R paper, not the similarly named human-to-robot handover dataset.
这里讲的是面向任务的 DexH2R，而不是同名的人机物体交接数据集。

73
00:06:32,329 --> 00:06:37,368
Its goal is completing manipulation, beyond preserving the appearance of human finger motion.
它的目标是完成操作，已经超出了保持人体手指动作外观。

74
00:06:37,818 --> 00:06:43,938
TeleDexter separates offline reference preparation from its live teleoperation controller.
TeleDexter 把离线参考准备，与实时遥操作控制器分开。

75
00:06:44,498 --> 00:06:49,578
The original overview links human hand-object references to a learned co-tracking policy.
原论文总览把人体手物参考，连接到学习得到的共同跟踪策略。

76
00:06:49,998 --> 00:06:55,678
The operator supplies fingertip and object goals; the policy handles contact execution.
操作者给出指尖与物体目标，策略负责接触执行。

77
00:06:56,238 --> 00:07:01,223
Consecutive subgoals allow some freedom in how the robot reaches each useful interaction state.
连续子目标允许机器人保留一定自由度，选择怎样到达每个有效交互状态。

78
00:07:01,238 --> 00:07:07,338
The paper uses marked gloves and optical motion capture, with a separate pregrasp control phase.
论文使用带标记的手套和光学动捕，并单独设置了抓取前的控制阶段。

79
00:07:07,678 --> 00:07:12,858
Replacing that input with bare-camera tracking requires fresh validation of the complete system.
把这些输入换成无穿戴摄像头追踪，需要重新验证完整系统。

80
00:07:13,349 --> 00:07:18,609
Choose a kinematic mapper when you need responsive joint references for an operator.
需要给操作者提供响应及时的关节参考时，先选择运动学映射器。

81
00:07:19,069 --> 00:07:24,969
Choose offline physical transfer when you need executable demonstrations from recorded human motion.
需要把记录的人体运动变成可执行示范时，再考虑离线物理迁移。

82
00:07:25,389 --> 00:07:30,569
Choose a feedback controller when the robot must correct interaction errors as the task unfolds.
如果机器人要在任务进行中修正交互误差，就需要反馈控制器。

83
00:07:31,149 --> 00:07:37,629
Then evaluate the entire sequence: approach, establish contact, lift, transport, and release.
随后评价完整序列：靠近、建立接触、提起、搬运与释放。

84
00:07:37,909 --> 00:07:42,974
Keep the reference error, contact quality, task success, and real-world evidence separate.
把参考误差、接触质量、任务成功，以及真机证据分别记录。

85
00:07:42,989 --> 00:07:48,229
This reveals which component failed, and which comparison can actually answer your question.
这样才能知道哪个组件失败，以及哪种比较真正回答了你的问题。
